 "body": "## [F-NEW-169] dooz compose-navigation NPE chain \u2014 3 roots after rc=-11 fix\n\nWith the SIGSEGV root fixed (#345), dooz now runs gracefully (rc=1, 41/41\nframes, UI painted) but `MainActivity.onCreate` still dies at invoke_pc=317\nthrough deferred-unwind NPE chains. Remaining roots, in encounter order:\n\n| # | Symptom | Site | Likely law |\n|---|---------|------|-----------|\n| 1 | `Handler.postAtFrontOfQueue` on null receiver | `Lr;.onAttachedToWindow pc=50` | null Handler field source (postAtFrontOfQueue bridge itself landed) |\n| 2 | `Object.getClass` on null | `Lox0;.a pc=30` \u2192 `Leo;.V pc=44` | follows `Lej0;.<clinit>` `Field.get` null \u2014 reflection family |\n| 3 | `View.getWidth` on null | `Lt4;.L pc=112` (inside Lt4.onLayout) | compose measureAndLayout null child/field |\n\nPlus handled-but-degraded: `java.lang.reflect.Field.get` returns null\n(Lej0;.<clinit>, caught) \u2014 reflection static-field read family.\n\n## Definition of done\nEach root: AOSP/libcore source cited, minimal semantic law, real-APK\nevidence, 3-run repeatability. Exit when MainActivity.onCreate completes\nwithout APP-BOUNDARY unwind and the dooz board reaches interactive state.\n\n## Protocol\n- [x] open (this ticket)\n- [ ] root-cause root 1/2/3 (AOSP upstream cited)\n- [ ] fixes land (runtime laws, evidence-backed)\n- [ ] battery gate re-run (ALL PASS)\n- [ ] close with evidence comment",
